# Copy to prod.dashboard.env / dev.dashboard.env and fill in ON THE HOST.
# Gitignored, `chmod 600`.
#
# FILL BY NAME, ONE LINE AT A TIME. Never `cat` an infra .env into this file --
# env_file injects every line it finds, which would hand this container every
# other project's credentials on the box.
#
# The compose file already sets GAOS_ADDR, GAOS_ARCADE_URL, GAOS_ARCADE_DB and
# GAOS_COOKIE_SECURE, because those are topology rather than secrets and belong
# in a file you can diff. Only credentials live here.

# --- ArcadeDB ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The database is reached by container DNS on the shared infra network
# (arcadedb-master / arcadedb-master-dev), so there is no host and no port here
# -- only the credentials. Get them from the infra stack's own .env, by name.
#
# Wrong values do not fail at startup: the dashboard serves its fixtures either
# way. /api/healthz is what tells you, and it answers 503 with
# {"database":"unreachable"}. That is the whole reason the probe exists.
GAOS_ARCADE_USER=
GAOS_ARCADE_PASSWORD=
